## Execution harness

Selected topology: **${strategy}**. Use native Agent Teams when they are enabled in this session;
otherwise dispatch the same roles as isolated subagents. Both paths satisfy the same contract, and
which one answered changes nothing a reader of the report can observe.

Harness obligations, none of them optional:

- Every worker runs in its own context (`isolation: ${isolation}`). A worker never reads another
  worker's result, and never runs in the coordinator's context.
- Dispatch exactly the selected roles, once each: ${roles}
- Hold the `${join}` barrier. Record every expected role as `delivered` or `failed` before anything
  downstream runs. A missing result is a recorded failure, never a silently shorter report.
- Run later phases only after their declared `needs` are satisfied.
- Only the phase that declares the report artifact may write it.

The phase graph, the isolation and join policies and the record schemas are in
`contracts/${workflow}.workflow.toml`, which ships with this package.

